sequenceDiagram
  title Registering for an event when seats may run out
  actor S as Student
  participant P as Event page
  participant A as Server action
  participant R as Registration service
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant N as Notifications and email

  S->>P: Clicks Register
  P->>A: registerAction(eventId)
  A->>A: requireRole(STUDENT): session re-read from the database
  A->>R: registerForEvent(student, eventId, now)
  R->>D: BEGIN, SELECT event FOR UPDATE
  Note over R,D: Other changes to this event wait here,<br/>so seats can't be oversold
  D-->>R: Event row, now locked
  R->>R: Check window, eligibility, verified email, no duplicate
  R->>D: Count seats taken
  D-->>R: Seats taken
  alt A seat is free
    R->>R: Issue a signed ticket code
    R->>D: INSERT registration (CONFIRMED, ticket code)
  else Event is full
    R->>D: INSERT registration (WAITLISTED, next position)
  end
  R->>D: COMMIT, releasing the lock
  R-->>A: Outcome and emails to send
  A-->>P: "You're in", page refreshes
  P-->>S: Shows registered or number in line
  A->>N: deliver(emails) after the response
  N->>D: Save bell notification
  N-->>S: Email with QR ticket
